Source: pve-gpu-sched
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PVE GPU Scheduler Project <gpu-sched@proxmox.local>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 12), dkms
Standards-Version: 4.5.1
Homepage: https://github.com/tf-jordan/gpu_band_sched

Package: pve-gpu-sched-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms, linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-generic
Recommends: proxmox-ve
Description: GPU time-sharing scheduler for Proxmox VE / KVM (DKMS)
 Module kernel mdev (VFIO mediated device) qui intercepte les acces
 MMIO des VMs vers le GPU physique et les ordonnance via l'algorithme
 BAND (Bandwidth-Aware Non-preemptive Dispatcher).
 .
 Permet a plusieurs VMs de partager un meme GPU physique (NVIDIA ou AMD)
 sans licence vGPU, via un scheduling equitable pondere (WFQ).
 .
 Fonctionnalites :
  - Scheduling BAND avec Weighted Fair Queuing
  - Shadow page tables GPU (NVC0/GCN)
  - IRQ forwarding via eventfd
  - Support NVIDIA (Fermi+) et AMD (GCN+)
  - Jusqu'a 16 VMs simultanees
  - Outil CLI pour gerer les instances mdev

Package: pve-gpu-sched-utils
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, pve-gpu-sched-dkms
Recommends: proxmox-ve, qemu-server
Description: GPU time-sharing scheduler - management utilities
 Outils de gestion pour le module pve-gpu-sched :
  - pve-gpu-sched : CLI pour creer/supprimer/lister les instances mdev GPU
  - Configuration modprobe et service systemd
  - Integration Proxmox VE
